  "notes": "USAGE: Sense 2 (stress release) is very common in everyday speech, especially the phrase ストレス{発散|はっさん}. Sense 1 is more technical/scientific.\n\nMATHEMATICS: In math, {発散|はっさん} also means 'divergence' (opposite of {収束|しゅうそく} 'convergence').\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ストレス{発散|はっさん} (stress relief)\n- {熱|ねつ}/{光|ひかり}/エネルギーを{発散|はっさん}する (to emit heat/light/energy)\n- {発散|はっさん}{方法|ほうほう} (way to let off steam)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {放出|ほうしゅつ} (emission, discharge - more technical)\n- {解消|かいしょう} (elimination, relief - for stress)\n- {吐|は}き{出|だ}す (to let out, vent)",
